{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And He spoke.</b> Now the matter is stated in summary: for Aaron too will be an intermediary between him and Pharaoh, as will yet be explained; therefore both shared in the speaking:" "<b>And He charged them.</b> To go to the children of Israel and to Pharaoh king of Egypt. And Rabbi Yeshuah said that the sense of ויצום is that they not be angry with Israel if Israel do not heed them. And there is no need [for this]."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:08.469427221Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}